# The build context is the repo root (docker-compose.yml needs `backend/`
# visible), so without this every build would upload the whole working tree to
# the daemon — including `.git`, two `node_modules` trees, and an 85 MB fat JAR
# in `backend/target` that the image rebuilds from source anyway.

.git
.github
**/node_modules

# Build output. `backend/target` in particular: copying a host-built JAR into
# the context risks the image silently shipping whatever was last built locally
# instead of what the Dockerfile compiles.
backend/target
frontend/dist
frontend/.vite

# Nothing in the image needs these, and `.env` holds local credentials that
# should never end up in a layer.
.env
*.env
!docker/.env.example
Docs
Design
Report
drafts
integration-test
ops
tmp
output
test-server-credits.md

# Playwright/browser verification artefacts.
.playwright-mcp
